Stop exporting model-written and CLI-relayed text when content capture is off.
`gen_ai.agent.description` on a subagent span came from the Task tool's input — a
summary the model wrote of the user's request, like "Refactor the billing
reconciliation in payments/ledger.py" — and sat above the guard protecting the
delegation's prompt. A failed result's error text became the span status
description, which is exported regardless: an `invalid_request_error` body can
quote the request that produced it, and the SDK's own docs call only the status
code safe to log. The error subtype stays in `error.type`, and the error text
stays off spans that carry no content.
